.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL.AVAILABILITY_STATIC" "3JS" "August 14, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel.availability_static \- LanguageModel: availability()
static method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]availability()\f[B]\f[R] static method of the
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] interface returns a status identifier
indicating whether the browser\(cqs language model supports a given set
of configuration options, without creating a session or triggering a
download.
.PP
Use \f[CR]availability()\f[R] before calling
\f[CR]LanguageModel.create()\f[R] to determine whether the desired
configuration is supported.
This avoids initiating a session only to have it fail, and lets you
provide a meaningful fallback to users when the configuration is not
supported.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
LanguageModel.availability()
LanguageModel.availability(options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object that represents the base set of options used when checking
language model support.
Properties include:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]expectedInputs\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An array of objects representing the required input modalities and
languages.
Each object can include the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
An enumerated value indicating the content type.
Must be one of:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]text\f[R]
Plain text content.
.TP
\f[B]image\f[R]
Image content.
.TP
\f[B]audio\f[R]
Audio content.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-call\f[R]
A tool invocation issued by the model.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-response\f[R]
The result of a tool invocation.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]languages\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An array of strings containing \c
.UR https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc5646/
BCP 47
.UE \c
\ language tags (for example, \f[CR]en\f[R], \f[CR]fr\f[R],
\f[CR]ja\f[R]) representing languages that the session is expected to
handle.
The user agent uses this list to determine whether the model supports
the specified languages.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]expectedOutputs\f[R]
An array of objects representing the required output modalities and
languages.
Each object can include the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
An enumerated value indicating the content type.
Must be one of:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]text\f[R]
Textual content.
.TP
\f[B]image\f[R]
Image content.
.TP
\f[B]audio\f[R]
Audio content.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-call\f[R]
A tool invocation issued by the model.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-response\f[R]
The result of a tool invocation.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]languages\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An array of strings containing \c
.UR https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc5646/
BCP 47
.UE \c
\ language tags (for example, \f[CR]en\f[R], \f[CR]fr\f[R],
\f[CR]ja\f[R]) that the session is expected to output.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]tools\f[R]
An array of objects representing tools available to the AI.
Each object can include the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]name\f[R]
A string giving the tool a unique name the model uses to refer to it
when issuing a tool call.
.TP
\f[B]description\f[R]
A string describing what the tool does.
The model uses this description to decide when and whether to invoke the
tool.
.TP
\f[B]inputSchema\f[R]
An object containing a \c
.UR https://json-schema.org/
JSON Schema
.UE \c
\ that describes the tool\(cqs input parameters.
The model uses this schema to construct the arguments it passes to the
tool\(cqs \f[CR]execute\f[R] function.
.TP
\f[B]execute\f[R]
A callback function that the user agent invokes when the model calls
this tool.
It can receive any arguments provided by the model as appropriate and
returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with a \f[CR]String\f[R]
representing the tool\(cqs result.
.RE
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with one of the values listed below.
.TP
\f[B]available\f[R]
The model is ready to use with the given options.
.TP
\f[B]downloadable\f[R]
The model can support the given options but needs to download additional
data to do so.
The download has not yet started.
.TP
\f[B]downloading\f[R]
The model can support the given options with an additional data
download.
The download is currently in progress.
.TP
\f[B]unavailable\f[R]
The model cannot support the given options, or the user agent cannot
determine availability, for example, due to a transient activation
error.
In that case, the caller should retry or fall back to an alternative
implementation.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the calling document is not fully active.
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if usage of the method is blocked by a \f[CR]language\-model\f[R]
\f[CR]Permissions\-Policy\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
See also Using the Prompt API > Checking configuration support and the
Complete example on the same page.
.SS Requesting input support
This example shows how to determine whether text and image inputs are
supported by the model.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] status = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.availability({
  expectedInputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq }, { type: \(dqimage\(dq }],
});
.EE
.SS Checking availability for a specific language
This example tests whether the model supports English before asking it
to translate Japanese text to English.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] status = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.availability({
  expectedInputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq, languages: [\(dqja\(dq] }],
  expectedOutputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq, languages: [\(dqen\(dq] }],
});

\f[B]if\f[R] (status === \(dqavailable\(dq) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create({
    expectedInputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq, languages: [\(dqja\(dq] }],
    expectedOutputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq, languages: [\(dqen\(dq] }],
  });

  \f[B]const\f[R] translation = \f[B]await\f[R] session.prompt([
    {
      role: \(dquser\(dq,
      content: \(dqTranslate the following text into English\(dq,
    },
    {
      role: \(dquser\(dq,
      content: \(dq桜はきれいです\(dq,
    },
  ]);

  console.log(translation);
}
.EE
.SS Checking availability for multimodal input
Multimodal input describes sessions that can use more than one type of
input, such as text and images.
Since the availability of input types varies by language model, your
code should check the availability of desired modes before creating a
session.
An example is shown here.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] availability = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.availability({
  expectedInputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq }, { type: \(dqimage\(dq }],
  expectedOutputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq, languages: [\(dqen\(dq] }],
});

\f[B]if\f[R] (availability === \(dqunavailable\(dq) {
  console.warn(\(dqThis configuration is not supported.\(dq);
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create({
    expectedInputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq }, { type: \(dqimage\(dq }],
    expectedOutputs: [{ type: \(dqtext\(dq, languages: [\(dqen\(dq] }],
  });
}
.EE
